# Architecture boundaries

Canon (do not fork a second handbook):
`docs/governance/ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLES.md`,
`docs/governance/CODE_QUALITY_STANDARDS.md`,
`AGENTS.md`.

## Stay at one public monorepo

This repo is Stage 3 (`apps/*` + `packages/*` + `catalog/*`). Do not split
into multi-monorepo, microfrontends, Module Federation, or a second UI
framework without a new ADR. Desktop is one Tauri app, not a shell of remotes.

## Dependency direction

- Clients depend on `@intentloom/protocol` and public application contracts.
- `apps/desktop` must not import `@intentloom/application`, `@intentloom/core`,
  or `@intentloom/daemon`.
- Platform packages must not import `apps/desktop`.
- Rust (`src-tauri`) is transport, window, dialog, and daemon lifecycle only.
  Domain rules stay in application/protocol/validator.
- Generated adapters and `catalog/` derivatives are not hand-edited as truth.

## File budgets

Prefer production files ≤250 lines. Do not grow a file past 400 without a
documented exception. Extract a cohesive responsibility instead of adding
helpers dumps or unused layers.
